#: ../../source/reference/design/entities-and-output.md:1
msgid "Entities, and the output schema"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/entities-and-output.md:3
msgid ""
"*Implemented.* What the project models, and why the shape of the output "
"is treated as an invariant rather than as a formatting choice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/entities-and-output.md:6
msgid "`Extracted`: what comes out of a pipeline"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/entities-and-output.md:7
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`Extracted` is the union of the entity kinds the project models — equity,"
" bond, fund, fund assets, SFDR classification, ESG indicator, rename, "
"merge, management company, investments manager — **plus one member that "
"is not an entity at all**: the promise entries a pipe deposited "
"({doc}`promises`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/entities-and-output.md:11
msgid ""
"Putting promises in the same union is what lets a pipe say *\"this page "
"produced a value for someone else\"* through the ordinary return path, "
"rather than through a side channel that every segment would have to know "
"about."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/entities-and-output.md:15
msgid "The entity list is a modelling decision"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/entities-and-output.md:17
msgid ""
"Ten kinds, not a generic bag of key-value pairs. Each is a thing a reader"
" of financial reports asks about, and each has fields with types and "
"domains — a currency is a currency, a date is a date, a percentage is "
"bounded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/entities-and-output.md:21
msgid ""
"**Rejected: a generic row type** with untyped columns, which would have "
"absorbed any format without change. It would also have pushed every "
"question of meaning to the consumer: whether two rows describe the same "
"fund, whether a number is a percentage or a fraction, whether an empty "
"cell is zero or unknown. The value of this project is precisely in having"
" answered those, so a generic model would have given away the product to "
"save work on the engine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/entities-and-output.md:27
msgid "The schema is an invariant of the product"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/entities-and-output.md:29
msgid ""
"The row structures carry their **own** validation: the domain each "
"numeric field must fall in, and the key on which two rows count as the "
"same. That validation lives with the schema rather than with the code "
"that writes files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/entities-and-output.md:33
msgid ""
"The reason is a claim about *what kind of fact* it is. An output file "
"that violates one of these is **wrong even if every step that produced it"
" was right** — it is not a bug in the writer, it is a statement about the"
" world that cannot be true. Validation attached to the writing would be "
"checking the writer; validation attached to the schema is checking the "
"claim."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/entities-and-output.md:38
msgid "Three rules a consumer of the tables can rely on"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/entities-and-output.md:39
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"They hold across every profile, and they exist so nobody has to guess "
"({doc}`../../guides/user/output`):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/entities-and-output.md:42
msgid ""
"**Every CSV always has its header, even with no rows.** A table with "
"nothing in it is a header-only file, never a missing one — so *\"nothing "
"found\"* and *\"no such table\"* stay distinguishable. This is the rule "
"that costs the most to keep and is worth the most: the alternative makes "
"every consumer write a special case for a file that may not exist, and "
"get it wrong."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/entities-and-output.md:47
msgid ""
"**Headers are exact**, in text and in order. A consumer may index by "
"position."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/entities-and-output.md:49
msgid ""
"**An absent optional value is an empty cell** — never `None`, never "
"`null`, never `NaN` — and a floating-point number always carries at least"
" one decimal. One representation of absence, and numbers that never "
"change type between rows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/entities-and-output.md:53
msgid "One set of tables per run"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/entities-and-output.md:55
msgid ""
"Resolved entities accumulate across every page, every document and every "
"job, and are written **once**, at the end. Not per document, not per job,"
" and — critically — not per child process when jobs run in parallel: the "
"children send results back and the parent writes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/entities-and-output.md:59
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"That is why job-level parallelism could be added without changing what "
"batch mode produces. See {doc}`parallelism`."
msgstr ""

